title: Zinoviev against Radek
subtitle: The Executive meets in Moscow to decide who lost Germany.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1923 and month = 12 and comintern_member = 1 and crisis = 0 and congress = 0 and e23_quarrel = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 3
on-arrival: {!
Q.e23_q_rose = (Q.german_october == 2) ? 1 : 0;
Q.e23_q_called = (Q.german_october == 1 || (Q.german_october == 0 && Q.e23_october_done == 1)) ? 1 : 0;
Q.e23_q_never = (Q.e23_october_done == 0) ? 1 : 0;
Q.e23_q_refused = (Q.e23_october_refused == 1) ? 1 : 0;
RG.news('Moscow: Zinoviev and Radek clash over the German defeat', 3);
!}

= Zinoviev against Radek

The Presidium of the Executive sits for three nights in the first week of December, on the German question.

[? if e23_q_called = 1 : Zinoviev says the German Zentrale called off the rising at Chemnitz because a Social Democratic minister threatened to walk out of the hall. Radek says he was in Germany and Zinoviev was not, and that the retreat saved the party. ?][? if e23_q_rose = 1 : Zinoviev says the German Zentrale prepared the rising like a debating society and fought it like a trade union. Radek says a rising without the Social Democratic workers could only be lost, and that he wrote as much in September. ?][? if e23_q_never = 1 : Zinoviev says the German revolution went past the German party while it was drafting resolutions. Radek says the party is still alive, which is more than can be said of the Bulgarians. ?] [? if e23_q_refused = 1 : On one point they agree: the German party refused the Executive's plan in September. ?]

Everybody in the room knows that this is also about Trotsky, who has written that the leaders of the International share the blame. Stalin takes notes. [? if e23_patron = 1 : Zinoviev has been our friend since Lenin fell ill, and he expects that to count tonight. ?][? if e23_patron = 2 : Trotsky has been our friend since Lenin fell ill, and the triumvirs know it. ?][? if e23_patron = 3 : Radek has been our friend since Lenin fell ill, and he is the one in the dock. ?]

- @radek: Stand by Radek.
- @zinoviev: Vote with Zinoviev.
- @trotsky: Write to Trotsky.
- @judge: Say the German party will judge its own leaders.

@radek
subtitle: Radek is grateful. Zinoviev will make him pay for it, and us.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e23_quarrel = 1;
RG.ecci('radek', Q.e23_patron == 3 ? 16 : 10);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -12);
RG.setRole('radek', 'Accused of opportunism in Moscow');
!}

The German delegation says the Zentrale stands by what it did. Radek embraces them in the corridor. [? if e23_patron = 3 : He tells them he will not forget it, and he gives them the names of the two men on the German commission who can still be talked to. ?] In January he is taken off the German commission.

@zinoviev
subtitle: Moscow's majority. Zinoviev sends his own man to Berlin.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e23_quarrel = 2;
RG.ecci('zinoviev', Q.e23_patron == 1 ? 16 : 10);
RG.ecci('radek', -10);
Q.independence -= Q.e23_patron == 1 ? 2 : 6;
Q.comintern_rep = 'Dmitri Manuilsky';
RG.setRole('radek', 'Removed from the German commission');
!}

The resolution condemns "the opportunist leadership of the German October", and the German delegation votes for it. Dmitri Manuilsky takes Radek's place in Berlin. [? if e23_patron = 1 : Zinoviev lets the Zentrale choose which of its members will be named in the resolution. ?]

@trotsky
subtitle: The triumvirs will note who agreed with Trotsky.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e23_quarrel = 3;
RG.ecci('trotsky', Q.e23_patron == 2 ? 14 : 8);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -8);
Q.independence += 2;
!}

Our letter says the German party made mistakes, and so did the Executive that planned the October from Moscow. Trotsky quotes it in *Pravda*. Stalin's secretariat files a copy.

@judge
subtitle: Every member of the Executive will be offended.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e23_quarrel = 4;
Q.independence += 6;
RG.ecci('all', -5);
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 2;
!}

The German delegation says the German Central Committee will decide who was to blame and send its findings to Moscow afterwards. Zinoviev calls it a declaration of independence.
